  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "Evidence: Only two experiments are complete. RNA (pca_n2000, singleprofile) achieves 48.5% acc while image (resnet50, singleprofile) is very weak at 20.8% acc, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. Uncertainty: We have no information on whether the RNA representation itself can be improved—pca_n2000 is a simple linear projection, and it is unclear whether a learned, biologically-informed encoder (scvi_n200) would capture more discriminative structure. This experiment (config_004: rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200) changes only the RNA encoder relative to config_001, providing a clean one-variable comparison. It will clarify whether representation quality is a bottleneck: if scvi_n200 substantially improves accuracy, it justifies investing further in learned encoders and multimodal combinations built on them; if it does not, PCA-level representations may suffice and we can redirect budget toward profile setting, aggregation, or fusion. Under a limited budget, resolving this foundational question about the strongest modality's representation is the highest-information next step before committing to more complex multimodal or multiprofile configurations."
}

